<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The neural experts in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> are trained with PPO-Lagrangian <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>)</cite> for 20M environment steps, yet their test success rates still fall short of 100% for the following reasons. The MetaDrive safety environments occasionally generate rare but challenging scenarios that even a well-trained policy may fail to handle. In the Table Wiping task, the neural expert sometimes fails to remove one or two markings on the whiteboard, leaving a small patch of dirt uncleaned. In the Nut Assembly task, successful grasping requires the gripper to be precisely aligned with the metal ring’s handle, which is highly sensitive to even minor action errors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Demo Video</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have attached our demo video to <a href="https://metadriverse.github.io/ppl" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://metadriverse.github.io/ppl</a>. This video shows how we conduct human experiments and the evaluation results of our method Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions (PPL). This video includes five sections:</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first section gives an overview of Predictive Preference Learning, showing what human observes on the screen and how human provides corrective demonstrations in an episode.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second section is the footage of the MetaDrive human experiment, where the human expert interacts with the driving agent via a gamepad.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The third section shows the evaluation results of the PPL agent in a held-out MetaDrive test environment. We compare our approach PPL with the PVP baseline <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>)</cite>, and both agents are trained to 10K timesteps. The evaluation results show that our approach PPL has a higher test success rate and lower safety cost.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The fourth section shows the applicability of our methods to manipulation tasks in Robosuite <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>)</cite>: Table Wiping and Nut Assembly. PPL successfully imitates the expert and accomplishes both tasks in evaluation environments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the fifth section, we provide a full training session on MetaDrive. The video is played at 5× speed, and it shows how a human expert trains a PPL agent on MetaDrive in under 12 minutes, with approximately 1.8K demonstration steps and 10K environment steps.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Human Subject Research Protocol</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Human Participants.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Five university students (ages 20–30) with valid driver’s licenses and video gaming experience took part in the study voluntarily. After receiving a detailed overview of the procedures and providing written informed consent under an IRB-approved protocol, each participant completed a hands-on familiarization session. During this session, they were informed how the predicted trajectories were shown on screen, and they practiced with our control interface and learning environments until performing ten consecutive successful runs before the main experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Main Experiment.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each participant began with one or two fully manual episodes to build confidence, and then ceded control to the agent when they felt safe. Participants were instructed to intervene only when the agent’s predicted trajectory appeared unsafe, illegal, or inconsistent with their desired actions. They were directed to prioritize safe task completion and then to guide the agent toward their personal driving or manipulation preferences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Notations</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before we prove Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Analysis ‣ 4 Method ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we recall all the notations in this work. We denote the human policy as <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and the novice policy as <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any stochastic policy <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> and the initial state distribution <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on state space <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the value function <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> as the expected cumulative return:
<math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})],</annotation></semantics></math>
wherein <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(s_{0},a_{0},s_{1},a_{1},...)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(s_{0},a_{0},s_{1},a_{1},...)</annotation></semantics></math> is the trajectory sampled from trajectory distribution <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the state transition distribution <math id="A5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also denote the Q-function of policy <math id="A5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q(s,a)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})\big|s_{0}=s,a_{0}=a]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s,a)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})\big|s_{0}=s,a_{0}=a].</annotation></semantics></math>
And we define the discounted state distribution under <math id="A5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\pi}(s)=(1-\gamma)\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}\mathbb{I}[s_{t}=s]]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\pi}(s)=(1-\gamma)\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{\tau\sim P_{\pi}}[\sum\limits_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}\mathbb{I}[s_{t}=s]].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our algorithm PPL, we have a preference dataset <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> containing preference pairs <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a^{+},a^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a^{+},a^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. The preference loss function of policy <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> in PPL is defined as</p>
<table id="A5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.111em">|</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant and <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)=(1+\exp(-x))^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)=(1+\exp(-x))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Sigmoid function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the state distribution in <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\text{pref}}(s)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{pref}}(s)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In addition, for any state <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{pref}}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{pref}}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote the empirical preference-pair distribution in state <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{pref}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\frac{\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s,a^{+}=a_{h},a^{-}=a_{n}]}{\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{pref}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\frac{\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s,a^{+}=a_{h},a^{-}=a_{n}]}{\sum\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which is a distribution on <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Analysis ‣ 4 Method ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to prove that the performance gap <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> between the human policy <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and the agent policy <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded by the following three error terms: the state distribution shift <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quality of preference labels <math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the optimization error <math id="A6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the total variation for any two distributions <math id="A6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math> on the same space as <math id="A6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\|P-Q\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\|P-Q\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we formally define the three error terms. The first state distribution shift error arises from the difference between the distribution of states in the preference dataset <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (denoted as <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{pref}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{pref}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>) and the discounted state distribution of the agent’s policy <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (denoted as <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\pi_{n}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\pi_{n}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>). To define the distribution shift error <math id="A6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}</annotation></semantics></math> in PPL, we use the total variation between the two distributions, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A6.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{dist}}=D_{\text{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{\text{pref}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>dist</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{dist}}=D_{\text{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{\text{pref}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The second error term arises from the misalignment of the positive actions in the preference dataset, as the human action <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> in each tuple <math id="A6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{s}_{i},a_{h},a_{n})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{s}_{i},a_{h},a_{n})\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled in state <math id="A6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> instead of the predicted future state <math id="A6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In an ideal preference dataset, one would observe expert and novice actions drawn directly at
<math id="A6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To quantify this error, we define the following distribution <math id="A6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{ideal}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\pi_{h}(a_{h}\mid s)\pi_{n}(a_{n}\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{ideal}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\pi_{h}(a_{h}\mid s)\pi_{n}(a_{n}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for any state <math id="A6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the distribution over pairs <math id="A6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{h},a_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{h},a_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> if both policies were sampled at directly at state <math id="A6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we use</p>
<table id="A6.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{pref}}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\text{pref}}}D_{\text{TV}}(\rho_{\text{ideal}}^{s},\rho_{\text{pref}}^{s})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{pref}}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\text{pref}}}D_{\text{TV}}(\rho_{\text{ideal}}^{s},\rho_{\text{pref}}^{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">to define the errors in the preference dataset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we define the optimization error of the agent policy <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A6.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi_{n})-\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi_{h})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi_{n})-\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi_{h}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Under these notations, we have the following Thm. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem F.1 (Formal Statement of Theorem ). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>. We note that when we choose a small <math id="A6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq M^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq M^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Thm. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem F.1 (Formal Statement of Theorem ). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A6.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot O\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+4\log 2\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}}{2\beta}}+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot O\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+4\log 2\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}}{2\beta}}+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Formal Statement of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Analysis ‣ 4 Method ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We denote the Q-function of the human policy <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume that for any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|Q^{*}(s,a)-Q^{*}(s,a^{\prime})\right|\leq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|Q^{*}(s,a)-Q^{*}(s,a^{\prime})\right|\leq U</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\log\pi_{h}(a|s)-\log\pi_{h}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\log\pi_{h}(a|s)-\log\pi_{h}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\log\pi_{n}(a|s)-\log\pi_{n}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\log\pi_{n}(a|s)-\log\pi_{n}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,M</annotation></semantics></math> are positive constants.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}}{2\beta}+\frac{\beta M^{2}}{8}}+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}}{2\beta}+\frac{\beta M^{2}}{8}}+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key is to combine Lem. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma F.2 (Performance Optimality Gap on the State Distribution Shift). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, Lem. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma F.3 (Misalignment of Preference Pairs). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, and Lem. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4 (Optimization Error Bounds the Total Variation). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a> to obtain the bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Lem. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma F.2 (Performance Optimality Gap on the State Distribution Shift). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, we can use the state distribution shift and the total variation of the two policies <math id="A6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h},\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h},\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> to bound the optimality gap:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>dist</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, for any policy <math id="A6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the function</span></p>
<table id="A6.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which represents the preference loss on ideal preference pairs, where <math id="A6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{+},a^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{+},a^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> are sampled directly at each state <math id="A6.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4 (Optimization Error Bounds the Total Variation). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a>, we can bound the total variation term <math id="A6.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)\leq\sqrt{\frac{g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})}{2\beta}+\frac{\beta M^{2}}{8}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)\leq\sqrt{\frac{g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})}{2\beta}+\frac{\beta M^{2}}{8}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, by Lem. <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma F.3 (Misalignment of Preference Pairs). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, we can also bound <math id="A6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> by the optimization error <math id="A6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the misalignment of preference levels <math id="A6.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})\leq\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})\leq\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. <a href="#A6.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, <a href="#A6.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, and <a href="#A6.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> yields Eq. <a href="#A6.E14" title="In Theorem F.1 (Formal Statement of Theorem ). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Performance Optimality Gap on the State Distribution Shift)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We recall that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pref</mtext></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s]</annotation></semantics></math>, and we define <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for any two stochastic policies <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h},\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h},\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>dist</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}=D_{\mathrm{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{{\mathrm{pref}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}=D_{\mathrm{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{{\mathrm{pref}}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A6.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key is to use the Performance Difference Lemma (Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma G.2 (Performance Gap Between Human Policy and Novice Policy). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>) on <math id="A6.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding Eq. <a href="#A6.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>. Then, we can apply Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Expectation Difference via Total Variation). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, which bounds the expectation on <math id="A6.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim d_{\pi_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim d_{\pi_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the distribution shift term <math id="A6.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, applying the assumption <math id="A6.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|</annotation></semantics></math> bounds the difference of the Q-function by the total variation between <math id="A6.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the Performance Difference Lemma (Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma G.2 (Performance Gap Between Human Policy and Novice Policy). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\pi_{n}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\pi_{n}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Expectation Difference via Total Variation). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, as <math id="A6.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\pi_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\pi_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}</annotation></semantics></math> are two distributions on the same state space <math id="A6.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\gamma)(J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\gamma)(J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E21Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2D_{\mathrm{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{{\mathrm{pref}}})\cdot\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\left|\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2D_{\mathrm{TV}}(d_{\pi_{n}},d_{{\mathrm{pref}}})\cdot\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\left|\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E21Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E21Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\cdot\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>dist</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\cdot\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E21Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21Xe.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\left[\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]+2U\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>dist</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}\left[\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\right]+2U\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{dist}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">where we use <math id="A6.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\max\limits_{s\in\mathcal{S},a_{1},a_{2}\in\mathcal{A}}\left|Q^{*}(s,a_{1})-Q^{*}(s,a_{2})\right|</annotation></semantics></math> in the last inequality of Eq. <a href="#A6.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, <math id="A6.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{n}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{n}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> are two probability distributions on the same action space <math id="A6.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Expectation Difference via Total Variation). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, we have for any <math id="A6.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\leq U\cdot D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{h}\sim\pi_{h}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{h})-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a_{n}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}Q^{*}(s,a_{n})\leq U\cdot D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proves that</span></p>
<table id="A6.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{h})-J(\pi_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>dist</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{U}{1-\gamma}\cdot\Big(\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(\pi_{h}(\cdot|s),\pi_{n}(\cdot|s)\big)+2\delta_{\mathrm{dist}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.3</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Misalignment of Preference Pairs)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We recall that the loss function of the policy <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)=-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s,a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)=-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s,a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
And the optimization loss is defined as <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{pref}}(\pi_{n})-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{pref}}(\pi_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{pref}}(\pi_{n})-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{pref}}(\pi_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition, following Eq. <a href="#A6.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, for any policy <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</span></p>
<table id="A6.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi)=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}\left[-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumption that for any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\log\pi_{h}(a|s)-\log\pi_{h}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\log\pi_{h}(a|s)-\log\pi_{h}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\log\pi_{n}(a|s)-\log\pi_{n}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\log\pi_{n}(a|s)-\log\pi_{n}(a^{\prime}|s)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we can bound</span></p>
<table id="A6.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})\leq\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi_{n})-g(\pi_{h})\leq\epsilon+4(\beta M+\log 2)\cdot\delta_{\mathrm{pref}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s},\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ideal</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{pref}}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{{\mathrm{pref}}}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s},\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A6.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key is to apply Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Expectation Difference via Total Variation). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> on the two distributions <math id="A6.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ideal</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that we can bound the difference of <math id="A6.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{pref}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> for any policy <math id="A6.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta_{\mathrm{pref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta_{\mathrm{pref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A6.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="A6.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\pi_{h}(a_{h}\mid s)\pi_{n}(a_{n}\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ideal</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\pi_{h}(a_{h}\mid s)\pi_{n}(a_{n}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math>, a probability distribution on <math id="A6.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also denote <math id="A6.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}(s,a_{h},a_{n})/d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}^{s}(a_{h},a_{n})=\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}(s,a_{h},a_{n})/d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{pref}}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where we recall that <math id="A6.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}(s,a_{h},a_{n})={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s,a^{+}=a_{h},a^{-}=a_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{pref}}(s,a_{h},a_{n})={|\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}|}^{-1}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(s^{\prime},a^{+},a^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\mathbb{I}[s^{\prime}=s,a^{+}=a_{h},a^{-}=a_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key is that <math id="A6.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ideal</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{s}_{\mathrm{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>pref</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{s}_{\mathrm{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math> are two distributions on the same space <math id="A6.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we can apply Lem. <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Expectation Difference via Total Variation). ‣ Appendix G Technical Lemmas ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> on Eq. <a href="#A6.E24" title="In Lemma F.3 (Misalignment of Preference Pairs). ‣ Appendix F Proof of Theorem ‣ Predictive Preference Learning from Human Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> to obtain the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">We denote <math id="A6.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})=-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})=-\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\pi(a^{+}\mid s)-\beta\log\pi(a^{-}\mid s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">We also denote <math id="A6.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\pi}_{\text{max}}=\max\limits_{s,a^{+},a^{-}}|l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\pi}_{\text{max}}=\max\limits_{s,a^{+},a^{-}}|l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\text{max}}=\max(l^{\pi_{h}}_{\text{max}},l^{\pi_{n}}_{\text{max}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mtext>max</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mtext>max</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\text{max}}=\max(l^{\pi_{h}}_{\text{max}},l^{\pi_{n}}_{\text{max}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any policy <math id="A6.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A6.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{a^{+}\sim\pi_{h}(s),a^{-}\sim\pi_{n}(s)}l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{s\sim d_{\mathrm{pref}}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{(a^{+},a^{-})\sim\rho_{\mathrm{ideal}}^{s}}l^{\pi}(s,a^{+},a^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pref</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo>